# stompbox.world
#
# Every variable here is OPTIONAL. There is no database, no API key and no
# credential of any kind: the site is a static Next.js build over a hand
# written dataset, and it runs with this file absent entirely.
#
# Every value is trimmed on read, and a whitespace-only value counts as unset.
# See lib/env.ts for why.

# Canonical origin, no trailing slash. Used for canonical tags, Open Graph
# URLs, robots.txt and the sitemap. Defaults to https://stompbox.world, which
# is deliberately not localhost: a preview deploy with this unset should still
# emit absolute URLs pointing somewhere real.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://stompbox.world

# The Instagram handle in the footer and on the home page strip.
# Defaults to stomp_box_world. Note this is NOT the domain and NOT the older
# @stompbox.world grid: they are different accounts that read alike.
INSTAGRAM_HANDLE=stomp_box_world

# Post permalinks for the home page embed strip, comma or newline separated.
# Unset is the expected state and renders a plain follow callout instead of a
# row of empty boxes. Only real instagram.com /p/, /reel/ or /tv/ permalinks
# are accepted; anything else is dropped rather than handed to the embed
# script, because a bad paste renders as a broken site rather than an
# unconfigured one.
#
# INSTAGRAM_POST_URLS=https://www.instagram.com/p/XXXXXXXXX/,https://www.instagram.com/p/YYYYYYYYY/

# Origin of the sister site the catalogue is read from. Defaults to production.
GEAR_AVAIL_URL=https://gearavail.com

# --- The catalogue refresh hook (/api/revalidate) ----------------------------
#
# WHAT IT IS FOR. Both Vercel projects build from the same commit at the same
# time, and this one prerenders /catalog by fetching Gear Avail during its
# build. So this build can finish first and bake in a response from the OLD
# production deployment, which is exactly what happened once: the page shipped
# with the previous version's numbers and looked like the deploy had failed.
# Without this hook it corrects itself in fifteen minutes. With it, Vercel says
# "the sister site is live now" and the next request rebuilds the page.
#
# UNSET IS FULLY SUPPORTED. The route answers 503, and the fifteen minute
# window is the only refresh, which is where this site was before.
#
# NEITHER OF THESE IS A CREDENTIAL FOR ANYTHING. They only prove an inbound
# request is genuine. They reach nothing, and CLAUDE.md's rule against putting
# a credential in this project is about not giving it a way INTO the sister
# site's data.
#
# SETUP, once, in the Vercel dashboard:
#   1. Team Settings, then Webhooks, then Create Webhook
#   2. Endpoint: https://stompbox.world/api/revalidate
#   3. Event:    deployment.succeeded
#   4. Project:  musictime (the aggregator, NOT this one)
#   5. Copy the secret it shows once, and set it here on THIS project
# VERCEL_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Optional second way in, for forcing a refresh by hand or from a script:
#   curl -X POST https://stompbox.world/api/revalidate \
#        -H "Authorization: Bearer $REVALIDATE_SECRET"
# It is a separate value from the webhook secret on purpose. That one is only
# ever presented as a signature over a body, and accepting it bare as a token
# would make signing pointless.
# REVALIDATE_SECRET=

# Which Vercel PROJECT's production deploys refresh the catalogue. Defaults to
# musictime, which is the aggregator's project name and is NOT its domain: it
# predates the site being called Gear Avail. Set this if that project is ever
# renamed, or the webhook will arrive and be ignored as somebody else's deploy.
# GEAR_AVAIL_PROJECT=musictime
